he gates to secure coveted places in the festival tents.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>German police probe arson attack on Wuppertal synagogue</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:37134173414646a351c117d28fd037f6de0e3c0c0b7a12e951893c35cdb2a4e9</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T15:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-police-probe-arson-attack-on-wuppertal-synagogue/a-79331270--dce70b32746f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-police-probe-arson-attack-on-wuppertal-synagogue/a-79331270?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The man detained shortly after allegedly trying to set fire to Wuppertal's synagogue made antisemitic comments to the arresting officers, prosecutors say. The 37-year-old Afghan citizen also had knives in his apartment.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>In cosmopolitan Berlin, elections still closed to foreigners</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9f17de51251260307333575376a4c495404ddbc6714bae64e99dd8fdb83f844d</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T07:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/in-cosmopolitan-berlin-elections-still-closed-to-foreigners/a-78744579--2c7a3b66c58f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/in-cosmopolitan-berlin-elections-still-closed-to-foreigners/a-78744579?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A quarter of Berlin residents will have no say in the German capital's city-state election because they lack citizenship. That's the highest proportion of residents excluded from the election yet, and many are unhappy.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: Is it possible to replace the chancellor?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:90738258b231ea1e1db52db5cb7cf5d93fe6cd23f3e9f41074e07fb273aa2808</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:16Z</updated><pub